---
name: Synchronize a domain feed into HarfangLab
description: |
  Downloads a plain-text feed of malicious domains every hour, keeps the
  domains in the `threat-domains` lookup table for enrichment, and
  synchronizes them into the HarfangLab IOC source `tenzir-threat-domains`.
  Domains that leave the feed are disabled in HarfangLab.

  Declare the lookup table in the configuration as
  `contexts/threat-domains.yaml` with `type: lookup-table`, and give it a
  write timeout so that domains that leave the feed also leave the table.

  The first run creates every domain with one request, which takes about
  40 minutes for 10,000 domains. The hourly runs then only write the
  differences. Don't load the feed with the Manager's CSV import instead,
  because it creates blocking IOCs.

  Pruning stops the run before any write when it would disable more than
  10 IOCs and more than 10% of the source, for example after a truncated
  download. Raise `max_prune_share` for a feed that changes faster. Watch
  for `failed` results, and for the pipeline stopping on an error.
---

every 1h {
  from_http "https://feeds.example.org/malicious-domains.txt" {
    read_lines
  }
  line = line.trim()
  where line != "" and not line.starts_with("#")
  this = {domain: line}
  fork {
    context_update "threat-domains", key=domain
  }
  harfanglab::ioc::sync "https://example.hurukai.io:8443",
    token=secret("harfanglab-api-token"),
    source="tenzir-threat-domains",
    type="domain",
    value=domain,
    prune=true,
    max_prune_share=0.1
  where action == "failed"
}
